From 1a7012fea4a35f0b206fc2ffe3cd4a584f6c8038 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 11:58:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 754/913] dts: stm32: remove system_off_soc in pwr node of
 stm32mp1

Remove support for the proprietary "system_off_soc_mode" property in
the PWR node, as shutdown is now handled through the
"system-power-controller" property in the PMIC node for the STPMIC1
and STPMIC2 families (STPMIC1L, STPMIC2 and STPMIC2L).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 10457186f87aa9ba426e36ca4445e0981a2fd55d dts: stm32: remove system_off_soc in pwr node of stm32mp1]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I8cff66d36b78abbd36cb6433d86bcadf55748190
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/581305
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
